Detailed Technical Implementation Planning
Repository / Module
Strategic Focus
GitHub Implementation & Engineering Milestones
oidc-ssi-bridge
Core Protocol Gateway
• Standard Mapping Engine: Build bi-directional translators mapping OAuth2/OIDC claims to DIF Presentation Exchange (PEX) & Digital Credentials Query Language (DCQL) queries.

• Session Management: Implement stateless, distributed nonce caches using Redis to secure cross-device OID4VP handshakes against replay vectors.

• CI/CD Automation: GitHub Actions pipeline running automated security fuzzing, automated dependency scanning, and conformance test suites against the official EU Digital Identity Wallet reference specs.
enterprise-rp-sdk
B2B Adoption Tooling
• Lightweight SDKs: Package client-side verification libraries in TypeScript, Python, and Go for enterprise relying parties.

• Zero-Knowledge Proofs (ZKP): Deliver out-of-the-box support for selective attribute disclosure (e.g., verifying age or accreditation without leaking full PII).

• Documentation & Playground: Maintain an interactive developer portal hosted via GitHub Pages with live test credentials and sandbox wallet connectors.
agent-trust-mesh
Decentralized AI Governance
• Cryptographic Agent Passports: Implement verifiable identity bindings for autonomous AI agents, ensuring LLM nodes sign requests using hardware-backed keys or DIDs.

• Audit Logs: Immutable, append-only credential verification logs to prevent prompt injection and synthetic impersonation in multi-agent workflows.

Repository Operations & Governance Blueprint
To maximize community trust, open-source adoption, and enterprise viability, the GitHub organization should enforce the following engineering workflows:
Specification-First Development:
Align all protocol implementations with emerging W3C, OpenID Foundation (OID4VP/SIOPv2), and eIDAS 2.0 technical profiles. Track changes via public RFC-style Markdown documents in a dedicated specs repository.
Cryptographic Compliance and Security Audits:
Integrate continuous vulnerability scanners (e.g., Trivy, SonarQube, and custom DID resolver unit tests) into GitHub Actions pull request checks.
Mandate Signed Commits (GPG/SSH) across all core maintainers to ensure complete supply-chain integrity for enterprise clients.
Automated Release and Semantic Versioning:
Utilize automated tagging and changelog generation (semantic-release) to push stable bridge binaries and SDK packages to public and private package registries (npm, PyG, Maven) instantly upon merge to main.
